<title>CANADA: Onex CEO may sell some shares.</title>
<headline>Onex CEO may sell some shares.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Onex Corp said on Monday that Chief Executive Gerald Schwartz filed notice with the Ontario Securities Commission that a corporation he controls may sell up to 700,000 subordinate voting shares of Onex through the Toronto Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Onex said the transactions would not materially affect Schwartz's control position in Onex. The shares that may be sold represent about eight percent of the shares Schwartz beneficially owns.</p>
<p>The company said that Schwartz had in the past sold shares at this time of year and that part of the proceeds would be used to pay taxes.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416-941-8100))</p>
</text>
